## Commit Standards

### Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<optional body - what and why, not how>

Assisted by: Claude Code - <model>
```

Always use `git commit -s` to add "Signed-off-by" trailer automatically.

### Types

- `feat`: New feature
- `fix`: Bug fix
- `refactor`: Code restructuring
- `test`: Adding/updating tests
- `docs`: Documentation
- `chore`: Maintenance tasks

### Rules

- Subject line: imperative mood, no period, max ~72 chars
- Body: explain what and why, not how
- Always include the "Assisted by: Claude Code - <model>" trailer (e.g. `opus-4.6`, `sonnet-4`)
- Never use `git add -f` to bypass .gitignore
- `.ai/` tracked subdirectories (specs, test-plans, decisions) can be staged normally; other `.ai/` dirs (plans, checkpoints, exploration, reviews, research) are gitignored and must stay local
